  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name='Appendix'>
      <repository-location id='Appendix' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/OccasionPenetration' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='text-align' id='dash-text_19' value='center' />
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_19' value='center' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1400' maxwidth='1400' minheight='1400' minwidth='1400' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='95287' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='4142'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Occasion Penetration Report</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> shows different metrics (such as orders, sessions or customer data) for each occasion on a monthly basis. City and country granularity.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The report consists on the following tabs:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>(1) </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Occasion - Time of the day:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> City and Country level view of different metrics based on occasions defined by the hour in which the order was placed.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>(2) </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Occasion - Verticals:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> City and Country level view of different metrics based on occasions defined by store type. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>(3) </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Occasion - Delivery Type:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> City and Country level view of different metrics based on how the order was delivered. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>__________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='6'>g</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='16'>Æ                                                                                                                             </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='16'>K</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='16'>                KPIs</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>__________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>1. Total Orders</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Successful Orders</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: -</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>2. Active Customers</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Customers who placed an order within the month under analysis.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Considering that one customer can place an order in multiple occasions (eg. breakfast, lunch and dinner), then the customer is considered in each one of those occasions. Therefore, it is not correct to obtain the total number of active customers per city by summing the number of customers on each occasion, because there will be duplicated values.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>3. % Total Active Customer City / Country</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Active Customers (per occasion) / Total Active Customers (per city or country - not duplicated).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>In order to get this result, it is important to obtain the total number of Active Customers per city or country, depeding on the granularity you are working with. As mentioned previously, instead of summing each occasion to get the total number of customers (which will have duplicated values), this KPI is calculated considering only single customer values, thus avoiding duplication. For this reason, the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>SUM of % Total Active Customer per City or Country is not 100%</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> -- In other words, it represents the percentage of Active Customers per occasion compared to the real base of Active Customers for that particular city or country. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>4. Active Frequency</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Successful Orders / Active Customers</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: -</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>5. Total Base</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Acumulative total number of customers per each occasion. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Considering that one customer can place an order in multiple occasions (eg. breakfast, lunch and dinner), then the customer is considered in each one of those occasions. Therefore, it is not correct to obtain total base per city by summing the total base for each occasion, because there will be duplicated values.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>6. Frequency</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Successful Orders / Total Base. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> -</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>7. Activity Rate</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Active Customers / Total Base </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> -</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>8. Acquisitions</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Number of customers that placed their first order ever. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Central DWH</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Even though a customer can place an order in different occasion (eg. lunch and dinner), it will be considered only in the occasion where the first order was placed. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>9. Sessions</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Total number of sessions. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Product Analytics</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> -</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d61f26' fontsize='10'>10. CVR</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Definition:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Successful Orders / Total number of sessions. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Data Source:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Product Analytics</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Comments: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> -</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='0' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='3571' id='19' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='571'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='18'>APPENDIX</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='0' />
              <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
